WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.260
I’m glad to see that you’re all okay.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.140
Yeah, that was a narrow escape from death.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.180
Yeah.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.480
It’s all thanks to Old...
I mean, Mister Pierrot.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.810
You’re back!

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.450
Thank goodness.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.990
Wh-What’s that?!

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.450
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.370
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.620
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.920
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:41.100
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.600
The King’s Question!!

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.490
Who is the first person you feed your delicious-looking bread to?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.860
It’s good to be alive.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.950
Well then, nature calls...

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.420
You there, what insolence!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.880
Do you wish to be shot?!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.430
Stop that.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.380
Put your guns away.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.930
Yes, Sir!

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.390
Our deepest apologies, Your Majesty.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.390
Y-Your Majesty?!

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.600
Stand back, you insolent fool!

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:50.270
This is the 14th King of Monaco, Leon Hart XIV!

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.650
Th-The King of Monaco?!

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.400
I had heard that the kings of Monaco

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.280
have worn a symbol of rank, the
“Lion’s Crown,” for generations...

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.160
but I didn’t know that it covered their entire face...

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:02.660
Your Majesty,

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.460
I actually have something I wish to report.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.420
Go on.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:10.290
Both the recent incident concerning the
stranding of the Japanese representatives

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.670
and the earlier case of the
sabotage at the deserted island

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.430
appear to have been carried out by Chairman Yulrich Rame of the Management Committee.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.840
Just as I had heard.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.600
You knew?!

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.390
Had Your Majesty already heard of this?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.810
As of yesterday, Rame has disappeared.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:30.770
What?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.530
We believe that he has fled abroad.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:38.990
Having heard beforehand that you, the secret police, had definite evidence against him,

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.950
he took action.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:42.820
No way...

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.750
Hello, Mama?

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.790
It’s me. Me.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.290
No, this is not a furikome sagi.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.130
Leaving that aside...

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.510
Mama, please don’t look for me.

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:00.730
If I’m found, I won’t be let off easily.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.760
Therefore...

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.100
I’m really sorry to say that

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.980
Rame has left behind a statement regretting the trouble he has caused all of your countries,

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.270
and has disappeared.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.400
I do not ask that you forgive Rame.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.900
However, I ask that you let bygones be bygones

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.780
and continue the tournament as planned.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:26.790
Henceforth, I will personally take over the proceedings,

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.660
and make certain that there are no irregularities.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.670
I pledge upon the honor of our Royal
Family that we shall have a fair tournament.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:38.260
To come here personally, just to atone for
the mistakes of one of your subordinates...

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:41.130
The King of Monaco is quite the samurai.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:42.640
Yeah.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.770
He forgave me, even though I pissed on him, after all...

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.690
But we might have been better off if
someone like you had just been shot.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:51.640
Why are you so...!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.940
Hey, Mister Kuroyanagi...

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:55.650
Hmm?

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:01.200
Won’t Old... I mean, Mister Pierrot be kind of lonely having reactions all by himself?

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:02.690
Of course not.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.160
That’s a good thing.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.200
I understand.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.910
It has been decided, Your Majesty.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:14.710
We have America, China, France
and Japan proceeding to the semifinals.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.710
All right!

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:23.220
Then, I will announce the topic of the semifinals for the four countries that were selected.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:28.810
For the drivers competing in next
week’s F1 Grand Prix in Monaco...

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:31.220
you must all make a “sports bread.”

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.680
A sports bread?!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.440
Does he mean a bread that does sports?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.610
Maybe...

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:37.730
Like that’s possible!

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:43.240
The matchups and detailed rules will be
explained to you after we return to Monaco.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:43.730
That is all.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.920
With this, we are finished with the quarterfinals.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.950
I heard.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:50.790
Pantasia Shinjuku Central Branch

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.910
So he disappeared, eh?
Pantasia Shinjuku Central Branch

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.130
To place the blame on Rame when it
looked like you might have been caught...

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.670
You’re really quite good.

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:01.630
Oh, what are you talking about?

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.920
You’re cute when you play dumb...

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:08.350
So, what are you going to do about the cockroaches?

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.930
At this rate, they’ll just go to the semifinals.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.930
You don’t need to worry.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.930
We just have to make sure that they don’t win.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:17.440
There are many other ways of doing that.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.520
Is that so?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.440
I guess I’ll relax, then.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.160
I’ll leave Monaco to you.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:28.400
But...

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.410
Cockroaches must be exterminated at the source.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:37.960
Hey!

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.750
The refrigerator’s broken.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.380
Get a new one.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.420
Y-Yes, Ma’am!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.920
I’ll do things my way here.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:51.930
In order to crush the nest of those cockroaches, the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:02.400
What kind of bread must we
make to get a sports bread?

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:05.900
A sports bread is like a sports drink.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.950
In other words, you need to make a
high-stamina, easily digestible bread.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.450
Oh?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.250
By the way, it seems that the winning bread

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:20.460
will be fed to the F1 racers at the opening ceremony of the Monaco Grand Prix.

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:27.920
It’s a job worthy of a baker.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:29.840
Yeah.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:33.220
There are various foods that can provide stamina.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.980
It’s fun just thinking about what ingredients to use.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:38.940
Yeah.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:43.230
You don’t seem very interested, Azuma...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.940
That’s not true.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.440
It’s just that I’ve already made something like this.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.450
<i>Japan</i> #51.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.740
Not again...

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:02.090
Moreover, #51 is so good that there
really isn’t anything I can do to improve it.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:02.710
Is that so?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.800
Too bad, eh, Suwabara?

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.630
It looks like we don’t have much to do this time, either.

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.930
A ha ha ha.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:09.730
No, that isn’t the case.
A ha ha ha.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:11.210
No, that isn’t the case.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:14.140
For the semifinals, each person makes a different bread.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.720
So as a team, you can make three kinds of bread.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:23.480
Apparently, the team to make the best bread will win.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.580
So even we can make breads?!

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:28.190
Guys!

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.740
Your opponent for the semifinals has been decided.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.700
It’s France.

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.580
Your opponent will be the Kaysers.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.090
A playoff against those masked guys, huh?

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:48.760
Interesting!

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.050
We’ll settle this!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:51.590
That’s right.

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.590
The totem-pole siblings can’t stand up to us.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.980
If we beat those fakes, your
store will do better as well, right?

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.100
We’ll take care of it, so leave it to us!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.060
O-Okay.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.440
Hey there,

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.190
we’ve come to the semifinals on account of our skill.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.610
So trust in us a little more.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.530
Yeah, leaving Baldy aside,

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.200
it’s not possible for me and Azuma to lose.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.160
Don’t worry.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.120
Who you calling Baldy?!

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.420
It’s true that you’re strong.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.120
But...

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:26.830
The oldest Kayser, Gran, is special.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:33.840
There probably isn’t a baker in the
world who can compete with him normally.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.340
Do you know why he never
talks, and is at the highest position?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:40.370
Because it’s comfortable?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.350
Because he likes heights!

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:45.610
He’s at the top so that

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:49.190
he never has to use the muscles in his legs or mouth,

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.860
since those aren’t used to bake bread.

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:52.610
What do you mean?!

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:57.530
The human brain has various
nerves traversing through it.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.540
It’s made such that unused skills atrophy,

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.920
and well-used skills are strengthened.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.540
Gran doesn’t speak or walk.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:10.120
So, only his hands are developed, since they’re needed to make bread.

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.630
You understand now, right?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.630
The eldest son Gran’s strength is the real thing.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.600
If you let down your guard, there’s no way you’ll win.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.390
All of you must get together to take him on.

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:21.850
All right.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.350
You’re right.

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.230
Understood.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.860
Suwabara, where are you going?

00:10:32.190 --> 00:10:33.610
Isn’t it obvious?

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:37.280
I’m going to train, in order to make the bread for the theme.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.450
Azuma.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.370
You, too, should not be satisfied that your bread has no room for change.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:47.370
You should instead be working hard to take that <i>Japan</i> #51 of yours to even greater heights.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.090
All right.

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.250
I’ll do my best, too.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.380
Azuma!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.260
Umm...

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:05.480
Umm... I guess I’ll go train, too.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:08.980
So, where are we supposed to go?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:25.740
The trio of Azuma, Suwabara, and Kawachi headed out to train for the semifinals.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.710
But they came back immediately.

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:31.500
What’s with you guys?

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.510
We forgot to ask you something.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:34.750
Forgot to ask me something?

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.760
I need a special ingredient for my bread.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.470
So where do I go to get it?

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:44.270
Go to the Monaco Royal Palace in such cases.

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:47.350
Ingredients from all over the
world have been collected there.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.110
They will be unconditionally
provided to all Monaco Cup participants.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.320
Understood.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.320
See ya.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.480
Later.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.980
And now, the three of them really went off to train...

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.990
Hey, get going already!

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:04.990
How do we get to the Royal Palace?

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:08.000
Ask all of the things you wish to know at once!

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:08.250
Aren’t you sad at not being able to do any reactions?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:08.870
Is the Royal Palace big?
Aren’t you sad at not being able to do any reactions?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:09.710
Kuro-yan...

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:10.920
Isn’t Kanmuri smarter than you?
Aren’t you sad at not being able to do any reactions?

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:11.290
Who are you in love with?
Kuro-yan...
Isn’t Kanmuri smarter than you?

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.380
Isn’t Kanmuri smarter than you?
Who are you in love with?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.500
How old are you?!
Who are you in love with?

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:17.840
I’d rather die than tell you!

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.840
Just go already!

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.180
Man...

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.510
I fear for the future.
Man...

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.520
Sophie Balzac Kirisaki-san.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.730
I am Pyramid Pharaoh, of the Monaco Secret Police.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.390
We have a few questions for you.

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:36.900
Regarding your father.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:45.410
Your father, Mr. Kirisaki Yuuichi, appears to be behind the disappearance of Mr. Rame.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.000
I wouldn’t be surprised if that demon
was responsible for something like that.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:51.670
Sophie...

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.920
Aside from the fact that Mr.
Kirisaki Yuuichi is the owner of St. Pierre,

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.670
he remains wrapped in mystery.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.140
Anything will do.

00:13:02.140 --> 00:13:07.150
Should you know anything
about Mr. Kirisaki, won’t you tell us?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.640
Wow! It’s huge!

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.570
Sorry about that.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.520
You are the Japanese representatives, right?

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.780
We have orders from His Majesty.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.830
Monaco Cup participants may pass.

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.490
Ah, thank you.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:28.530
Hey, wait.

00:13:28.910 --> 00:13:31.540
You can’t enter the Royal Palace with a sword.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.210
What?!

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.710
This Kaijinmaru is a warrior’s soul.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.420
It has assimilated with my flesh.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:39.800
Just try and take it from me!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.050
Sorry about that.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.480
Feel free to throw away this sort of thing.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.930
Wait, will you?!

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.300
Like hell I will!

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.770
You shouldn’t fight, okay?

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:49.770
Wait!

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:57.310
Amazing!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.730
Welcome, Japanese representatives.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:03.320
Various ingredients gathered from
all over the world can be found here.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.320
You can take whatever you like.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.700
Really generous, isn’t he?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.950
Yeah, he is.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.320
Yeah, a real man.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:12.870
However!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.830
Only if you can answer the question that I ask you.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:18.420
What was that?!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:24.090
That man abandoned my mother, my
brother and me when we were very young.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:27.970
I was raised without ever having seen my father’s face,

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.470
and then my mother passed away.

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.270
After a while, one day...

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.560
Sophie, Age 5

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:37.100
Silvan (soon to be Meister Kirisaki), Age 10

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:42.450
That man returned before us when we were starving.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.320
Papa?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.320
It’s Papa, right?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:50.080
Sophie, Papa’s come back!

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.820
You’ve come for us, haven’t you?

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:53.830
Silvan!

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:58.750
When you’ve made an
especially delicious-looking bread,

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:02.330
as a baker, who would you feed it to first?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.340
You’ve baked bread for us, haven’t you?

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.340
Thank you.

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:08.050
Answer my question.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.390
Huh?

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.140
That’s simple.

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:13.520
The answer is “your children,” right?

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:15.170
Incorrect.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:19.450
The answer is “yourself.”

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.970
I’ve come here just to eat
that especially delicious bread.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:35.590
After saying that, he stuffed his face with that
bread which looked delicious enough to die for...

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:41.340
and never appeared before us again.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.580
How inhuman!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.090
Kirisaki Yuuichi is a demon.

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.730
I’d rather die than forgive that man.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:50.840
I just can’t forgive him!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:53.840
So, here is the question.

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:58.730
When you have made an
especially delicious-looking bread,

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:02.850
who would you feed it to first?

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.320
What is your answer?

00:16:04.320 --> 00:16:06.700
Wh-What’s this?

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:09.200
That would depend on the person, right?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.860
Yeah, there can’t be a correct answer for this.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:20.830
Yourself!

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.880
The first one you feed it to is yourself.

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:28.880
Oh, my boy... Why do you say so?

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:32.850
Well, it <i>looks</i> like an especially delicious bread, right?

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:36.850
But, you don’t know whether or not it’s delicious, right?

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.150
You can’t feed something like that to someone else.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.890
Obviously, you have to eat it first.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:45.400
That is correct.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:50.400
This question teaches you that no matter how delicious-looking a bread you might have made,

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:56.830
you cannot feed it to someone else unless you have tasted it yourself.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:17:00.410
It was thought of by the owner of a certain bakery.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.410
I learned from this, and have adopted the policy myself.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:10.420
The bread from the semifinals will be
given to the top F1 racers of the world.

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:16.890
So, make a truly delicious bread that
you can be completely satisfied with.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:18.930
All right.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.650
Feel free to use any of the ingredients
collected here from all over the world.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:24.640
All right!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:27.110
Oh, this is rare.

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:28.610
I’m helping myself to this.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:29.360
This is it!

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:30.650
This is what I wanted!

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:33.950
In this manner, after obtaining the ingredients they desired,

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:38.160
the trio of Azuma, Kawachi,
and Suwabara left the Royal Palace

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:43.160
and set out on a journey to train
for the semifinals of the Monaco Cup.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:45.660
Or not..

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.460
What happened to the training?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:53.550
Don’t tell me you thought that I was going to seclude myself in the mountains to train, right?

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:55.550
Y-You’re not?!

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:57.430
Of course not!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.270
There’s a limit to nonsense.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:01.600
If I secluded myself in the mountains,

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.060
the ingredients would all rot without a fridge.

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.520
And, those who thought that
you’d go into the mountains...

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.400
Me!

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.060
Me!
Me!
Me!

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:10.400
Oh yeah, Kuro-yan...

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:14.820
You’d said that the Monaco Cup participants would receive the ingredients unconditionally.

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:16.620
But that wasn’t the case.

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:17.080
What?

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:20.160
The king asked us a strange question.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.350
“When you have made an especially
delicious-looking bread,

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:25.580
who would you feed it to first?”

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.960
It was a surprisingly deep question...

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.830
The King of Monaco asked you that question?!

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.340
I’m sorry...

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.880
W-What’s wrong...?

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:37.880
Actually...

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:41.890
You’re kidding!

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:45.100
How can someone do that to their own children?!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.400
What meaning is there in doing something like that?

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:52.900
If that’s the truth, then that
Kirisaki Yuuichi guy is no longer human.

00:18:52.900 --> 00:18:56.900
I really, really can’t forgive that old man.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:01.830
Well, it’s probably just a coincidence.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.910
But it just surprised us a little
to hear you asking that question.

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.000
No. It’s no coincidence.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:14.670
The king told us that he heard this
question from the owner of a certain bakery.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:18.180
Was he talking about the St. Pierre bakery?

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.770
It is probably just as Kawachi-san said.

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:22.680
What do you mean?

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:28.770
Actually, Kirisaki Yuuichi and His Majesty are what I suppose you would call best friends.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:32.190
The Monaco monarchy has an unusual tradition.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:34.650
According to the
Royal Family Code, Article XIV:

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:40.120
“As the lion does with its cub, the Child must
be dropped into a valley 1000 fathoms deep.”

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:41.580
So, for generations,

00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:45.620
the children of the Royal Family have been sent to be raised in the homes of the common folk.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.630
According to this rule, the present King of Monaco

00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:53.630
was raised as the child of a baker from age 8 to age 13.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.350
At that time, Kirisaki had come here from Japan for training,

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.140
and that’s when they seem to have met.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:02.350
But, Mr. Kirisaki suddenly disappeared

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:05.720
and then returned a few years ago.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:08.690
Is that why he asked that question...?

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:09.650
Yeah.

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.690
His Majesty probably does not have any ill intentions.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.730
But he trusts Kirisaki, and must have
asked the question upon his suggestion.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:19.230
But, why ask such a question?

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:21.240
It’s a warning.

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:22.700
Yeah.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:29.200
He’s saying, “Even without Rame, I can
crush you guys anytime. So be prepared.”

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:32.710
Wait! Why do you think that?

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:35.750
I agree that this Kirisaki
Yuuichi person isn’t trustworthy.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.970
But, why does he need to crush the Japanese team?

00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:42.260
You don’t need to know that, Kuro-yan.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.000
Even if I were to tell him that Yukino is hand in hand with Kirisaki

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:47.600
in trying to take over Pantasia...

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.480
Kuro-yan is from the Main Branch.

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:51.270
He can’t do anything.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:54.270
We have no choice but to fight it out ourselves.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.280
Why do I feel so alienated?

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:07.280
But, Kirisaki Yuuichi is a really fearsome man.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:11.790
I feel like a demon has grabbed ahold of my heart.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:15.630
How in the world do we stand up to a man...

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:18.970
who has the King of Monaco on his side?

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.750
We just have to bake bread.

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:22.510
Azuma...

00:21:22.510 --> 00:21:24.800
No matter how scary he is...

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:28.510
all we have to do is make a delicious bread, as usual.

00:21:30.190 --> 00:21:31.020
Yeah.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:32.800
The world we live in is a battlefield

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:36.520
into which only those who can bake truly good bread can enter.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.030
Bread is a sword.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:41.030
Only the best swordsmen can stay alive.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:43.530
No matter what schemes the enemy may come up with,

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.950
Azuma and I cannot be cut by such dirty swords!

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:50.530
All we have to do is fight fair and square.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.000
Just wait a moment!

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:52.920
Each and every time...

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.930
Why am I never included?!

00:21:55.420 --> 00:21:57.300
You’re still here?

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:58.000
Jeez.

00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:59.970
Always comparing each and every thing to swords...

00:21:59.970 --> 00:22:01.290
Dumb baldy...

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.050
Who you calling a baldy?!

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:05.010
You, of course!

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:08.350
Man, don’t fight.

00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:08.640
Your hairline is beginning to recede!

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.010
Feeling of alienation...

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:10.550
Your hairline is beginning to recede!

00:22:10.550 --> 00:22:11.730
What was that?!

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:14.940
Neither my brother nor I...

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:19.730
No, no baker has ever been
able to defeat Kirisaki Yuuichi.

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:21.520
But it’s strange...

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:23.610
The three of you are a bit of a joke,

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:26.240
but you just might be able to defeat that man.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.530
You make me feel that way.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:29.530
Ah, I got pulled in, too!

00:22:30.580 --> 00:22:33.950
Good luck, Japanese representatives!

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:08.670
Look. This is the proof that the Kaysers are the number one artisans in the world.

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:11.090
Can you imitate these guys?

00:24:14.310 --> 00:24:15.600
Of course not!

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.100
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:17.850
Curiouser and curiouser!!

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:18.980
The truth about the Kaysers!

00:24:18.980 --> 00:24:19.890
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:26.820
The word “sports” came to be used in
Japan toward the end of the Taisho era.
SPORTS

00:24:26.820 --> 00:24:29.770
At that time, only baseball, tennis, and other games that originated in the West

00:24:29.770 --> 00:24:31.660
were called sports.

00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.250
Oh?!
